/*!
\page page_stdedxpidtraits StDedxPidTraits

\brief PID traits storing dE/dx mean, uncertainty, method, and track length for a reconstructed track.

\section stdedxpidtraits_overview Overview

\ref StDedxPidTraits stores the ionisation energy-loss (dE/dx) measurement for a single
dE/dx estimation method (truncated mean, likelihood fit, etc.).  One instance per method
is attached to the track's PID traits vector.  The dE/dx signal in the STAR TPC is the
primary low-momentum PID discriminant (π/K/p separation up to ~1 GeV/c).

\section stdedxpidtraits_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackPidTraits
           └── StDedxPidTraits
\endcode

\section stdedxpidtraits_physics Physics Context

The mean dE/dx (\c mDedx, units GeV/cm) is computed from the charge deposited in TPC
pad rows using the Bethe–Bloch energy-loss curve.  The standard STAR method is the
truncated mean (top ~30% of samples removed).  Particle identification is performed
by comparing the measured value to the Bichsel-model prediction for each species.

\section stdedxpidtraits_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mNumberOfPoints | \c UShort_t | Packed: lower 2 digits = hit count; upper = track length (cm) × 100. |
| \c mMethod | \c Short_t | Encoded dE/dx method id (maps to \c StDedxMethod). |
| \c mDedx | \c Float_t | Mean dE/dx (GeV/cm). |
| \c mSigma | \c Float_t | Uncertainty on the mean. |
| \c mLog2dX | \c Float_t | log₂(⟨dX⟩) — mean segment length in log₂ units. |

\section stdedxpidtraits_methods StDedxMethod Values

| Enumerator | Description |
|---|---|
| \c kTruncatedMeanId | Truncated-mean estimator (standard). |
| \c kEnsembleTruncatedMeanId | Ensemble truncated mean. |
| \c kLikelihoodFitId | Likelihood fit (Bichsel model). |
| \c kWeightedTruncatedMeanId | Weighted truncated mean. |

\section stdedxpidtraits_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
for (const StTrackPidTraits* p : track->pidTraits()) {
    const StDedxPidTraits* d = dynamic_cast<const StDedxPidTraits*>(p);
    if (d && d->method() == kTruncatedMeanId) {
        double dEdx  = d->mean();            // GeV/cm
        double sigma = d->errorOnMean();
        int    n     = d->numberOfPoints();
        double len   = d->length();          // cm
    }
}
\endcode

\see StTrackPidTraits
\see StProbPidTraits
\see StTrack
*/
